sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Checking that all blocks of all lengths occur with equal frequency does not guarantee absence of regularity: sequences such as linear feedback shift register output or concatenated binary digits of successive integers have accurate block frequencies yet are non-random, as revealed for instance by an abnormally small spread of those frequencies.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Equal block frequencies of all lengths is not a universal randomness test";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 10, “Processes of Perception and Analysis”; section “Statistical Analysis” (from p. 588), p. 595. Scope: block-frequency tests for randomness of binary sequences"
}
